Archive email, chats, and meetings offline. Commands use the local daemon
(started on demand) or config.toml's [remote].url; --local forces local.

Start here: agent workflow
  msgvault setup status --json              # 1. inspect setup and missing capabilities
  msgvault account list --json              # 2. find accounts and source IDs
  msgvault source gmail add you@example.com # 3. connect a source; see source --help
  msgvault sync full you@example.com        # 4. first mail sync; later: msgvault sync
  msgvault search 'from:alice@example.com newer_than:30d' --json
  msgvault show <id> --json                 # 5. read a search result
  msgvault thread show <id> --json          #    read its conversation
  msgvault export eml <id> -o msg.eml        # 6. save a message
  msgvault export messages --start 2026-09-01T00:00:00Z --end 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z
  msgvault person --help
  msgvault daemon status

IDs and targets:
  Message IDs come from search's id field. show also accepts provider message
  IDs. Person, organization, source and generation IDs come from their list
  commands; deletion batch IDs come from deletion list. Collections use names.
  Accounts accept an identifier (email or source name); --source-id selects an
  exact source where supported. Use account list to resolve ambiguous names.
  --home overrides MSGVAULT_HOME (default ~/.msgvault); --config selects a TOML
  file. Agent-delegated mode uses --agent-url and --agent-token-file; restricted
  grants are issued by the owner with agent-token issue. See agent-token --help.

Output and errors:
  Human text is the default. Data commands offer --json where listed in their
  help; export messages writes JSON Lines. Success data stays on stdout.
  Diagnostics, progress and errors use stderr. Errors end with hint: <next step>.
  With --json, the final error is a JSON line on stderr:
  {"error":{"code":"usage","message":"...","hint":"...","exit_code":2}}
  Existing warnings/progress may precede it. --log-level=warn quiets routine logs.

Exit codes:
  0 success; 1 internal/unclassified; 2 usage (command/flags/argument count);
  3 invalid value; 4 not found; 5 not initialized; 6 conflict; 7 unavailable/auth;
  75 sync paused; 130 interrupted. A daemon may report paused as a sync outcome.

Environment:
  MSGVAULT_HOME selects the local home. MSGVAULT_IMAP_PASSWORD supplies an IMAP
  password. MSGVAULT_REMOTE_URL and MSGVAULT_REMOTE_API_KEY are used by account
  account export-token. VOYAGE_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY supply configured embeddings.
  MSGVAULT_ENABLE_REMOTE_DELETE is owner opt-in for remote deletion.
  Check a command's --help for its provider-specific setup and flags.

More workflows and examples: msgvault quickstart.

Usage:
  msgvault [command]

Search and read:
  chat        Find archived chats
  domain      List message domains
  label       List archive labels
  media       Search transcripts and mirrored document text
  meetings    Read archived meeting context, actions, and metrics
  query       Run a SQL query against the analytics cache
  search      Search messages using Gmail-like query syntax
  sender      List message senders
  show        Show full message details
  stats       Show archive message, thread, attachment and account totals
  thread      Show archived threads
  tui         Open the interactive terminal UI

Export:
  export      Export archived messages and attachments

People, organizations, and identity:
  attribute-definition Manage portable attribute definitions
  carddav              Manage CardDAV connections, books, and conflicts
  collection           Manage named groups of accounts
  employment           Manage employment records linking people and organizations
  identity             Manage the confirmed "me" identifiers for each account
  organization         Manage curated organizations and their employment records
  person               Find contacts and manage durable person profiles
  relationship-type    Manage person relationship types

Add and sync sources:
  account     List and manage source accounts
  source      Add and sync provider sources
  sync        Sync new mail from Gmail, IMAP, and Microsoft accounts
  verify      Verify archive integrity against Gmail

Import local exports:
  import      Import messages from local exports

Drafts, calendar, and Kata (write to providers):
  calendar    Control live calendar events and query availability
  draft       Create and manage provider drafts
  kata        Create Kata issues that quote archived evidence
  message     Manage archived messages

Review and delete:
  deduplicate Find and merge duplicate messages within an account
  deletion    Stage, review, and execute deletions
  gc          Purge source-deleted messages and compact the SQLite archive

Indexes, embeddings, and analytics cache:
  activity    Build the derived activity spine
  cache       Build and inspect the analytics cache
  documents   Manage document attachment indexing
  embeddings  Manage message vector embeddings
  eval        Score search quality against relevance judgments (qrels)
  fts         Maintain full-text search
  multimodal  Manage and search visual attachment embeddings

Maintenance and repair:
  attachment  Pack, restore, and maintain archived attachments
  backup      Back up the archive to a snapshot repository
  database    Initialize, migrate, and inspect the archive schema
  policy      Show room tiers and overrides
  repair      Repair archived messages and metadata

Setup, daemon, and integrations:
  agent-token Manage restricted agent grant tokens
  completion  Generate shell completion script
  credentials Manage provider credentials on the daemon host
  daemon      Manage the background daemon
  docbank     Manage the Docbank attachment mirror
  help        Help about any command
  logs        View and tail msgvault's structured log files
  mcp         Run MCP server for Claude Desktop integration
  openapi     Print the msgvault OpenAPI schema
  quickstart  Print a quickstart guide for AI agents
  serve       Run the archive daemon in the foreground
  setup       Run first-time setup; 'setup status' shows enabled features
  skills      Manage agent skills for coding assistants
  update      Update msgvault to the latest version
  version     Print version information

Flags:
      --agent-allow-insecure      Allow plain HTTP for agent-delegated connections (trusted networks only)
      --agent-token-file string   Path to a file containing the agent grant secret (requires --agent-url)
      --agent-url string          Daemon URL for agent-delegated mode (requires --agent-token-file)
      --config string             config file (default: ~/.msgvault/config.toml)
  -h, --help                      help for msgvault
      --home string               home directory (overrides MSGVAULT_HOME)
      --local                     use local daemon instead of configured remote
      --log-file string           override log file path (default: <data dir>/logs/msgvault-YYYY-MM-DD.log)
      --log-level string          log level: debug, info, warn, error (default: info)
      --log-sql                   log every SQL query at info level (verbose; for debugging)
      --log-sql-slow-ms int       threshold in ms above which a SQL query is logged as slow (default 100; 0 uses the default)
      --no-log-file               disable the log file for this run (stderr output stays on)
  -v, --verbose                   verbose output (implies --log-level=debug)

Use "msgvault [command] --help" for more information about a command.
